The issue occurs because Swag cannot find the definition for `errors.Error` type. We need to add proper model definitions that Swag can recognize and process.

## Steps:
1. Create Swagger model definitions for the API responses
2. Update the annotation responses to use these models
3. Adjust the run command to include proper directories

### c:\Users\Phu_Huynh\Desktop\ecom-go-learning\internal\handler\address.go

Let's add Swagger model definitions to the top of your address handler file:

````go
// filepath: c:\Users\Phu_Huynh\Desktop\ecom-go-learning\internal\handler\address.go
package handler

import (
	"ecom-go/internal/dtos"
	"net/http"
	"strconv"

	"ecom-go/internal/service"
	"ecom-go/pkg/errors"
	"ecom-go/pkg/http/response"

	"github.com/gin-gonic/gin"
	"github.com/go-playground/validator/v10"
)

// ErrorResponse represents an error response for swagger
// @Description Error response with message and details
type ErrorResponse struct {
	Code    int         `json:"code" example:"400"`
	Message string      `json:"message" example:"Bad request"`
	Details interface{} `json:"details,omitempty"`
}

// AddressResponse represents an address response for swagger
// @Description Address data response
type AddressResponse struct {
	ID          uint   `json:"id" example:"1"`
	UserID      uint   `json:"user_id" example:"1"`
	Name        string `json:"name" example:"Home"`
	Phone       string `json:"phone" example:"+1234567890"`
	Street      string `json:"street" example:"123 Main St"`
	City        string `json:"city" example:"New York"`
	State       string `json:"state" example:"NY"`
	PostalCode  string `json:"postal_code" example:"10001"`
	Country     string `json:"country" example:"USA"`
	IsDefault   bool   `json:"is_default" example:"true"`
}

// AddressListResponse represents a paginated list of addresses for swagger
// @Description Paginated list of addresses
type AddressListResponse struct {
	Data       []AddressResponse `json:"data"`
	Pagination PaginationInfo    `json:"pagination"`
}

// PaginationInfo represents pagination metadata for swagger
// @Description Pagination information
type PaginationInfo struct {
	CurrentPage int `json:"current_page" example:"1"`
	PerPage     int `json:"per_page" example:"10"`
	TotalItems  int `json:"total_items" example:"50"`
	TotalPages  int `json:"total_pages" example:"5"`
}

// SuccessResponse represents a general success response for swagger
// @Description Simple success response
type SuccessResponse struct {
	Message string `json:"message" example:"Operation successful"`
}

// @title E-Commerce API
// @description API for the E-Commerce application
// @version 1.0
// @BasePath /api/v1
// @securityDefinitions.apikey BearerAuth
// @in header
// @name Authorization

